        "heading": "Solo between the chords",
        "minutes": 3,
        "cells": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Press Play below to start the backing. When a chord comes round, strike its triad on beat 1, then fill the rest of the bar with a short line from the position. The ringed notes are the chord's own notes, so end the line on one of them.\nKeep going until the triad and the line sound like one phrase."
